Z||000000||DaveL||02-27-2001||03:41 PM||||The 2 little vertical black aluminum panels right behind the drivers and passengers windows of my 87 SE have badly faded paint. What would be the best type of paint to use to redo these?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||02-27-2001||05:02 PM||||I think the factory look was a semi flat black. I find for most of that type of touch up Krylon BBQ black works very well. It sticks pretty good on stainless and chrome too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mark||02-27-2001||06:25 PM||||I vote for Krylon semi-flat black.  Great stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000003||MrPBody||02-27-2001||07:26 PM||||Then there's Mar-Hyde satin black trim paint.  Easy to recognize -- it has a Fiero on the can.<BR>||||reg||1
